   'Riley honors U.S. Army Sgt. 1st Class Riley G. Stephens, 39, of Tolar, Texas, assigned to the 1st Battalion, 3rd Special Forces Group (Airborne). He died on Sept. 28, 2012, in Wardak, Afghanistan, of wounds caused by enemy small-arms fire.

You run 1.5 miles, do 150 burpees, then run another 1.5 miles. CrossFit adds that if you have a weight vest or body armor, you should wear it, but it gives no weight, so the vest is optional. There is nothing technical here. The challenge is the volume: 3 miles of running around a long block of burpees, and the second run starts on legs that have just done 150 squats to the floor and back.',
   '[{"name": "Run", "reps": "1.5 miles", "tip": "Run at a pace you could repeat after the burpees. Wear a vest or body armor if you have one."}, {"name": "Burpees", "reps": "150", "tip": "Chest to the floor and a small jump at the top. Pick a steady pace, such as 10 reps a minute, and hold it."}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "1.5 miles", "tip": "Shorten your stride for the first few minutes while your legs come back, then build the pace."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Start the first run slower than you want to", "Break the 150 burpees into sets with short, planned rests", "Note whether you wore a vest with your time"]'::jsonb,
   '["Treat the burpees as a long steady effort, not a sprint, because they make up most of the workout.", "Set a target such as sets of 10 with a few breaths between them, and keep it going all the way to 150.", "Step back and step up on the burpees when you get tired, rather than stopping for long rests.", "If you wear a vest or body armor, strap it tight so it does not bounce on the runs.", "Drink some water before you start, because this one can take close to an hour."]'::jsonb,
   'Go without the vest. Shorten each run to 1 mile or 800 m, and cut the burpees to 100 or 75. Newer athletes can step back and step up on every burpee instead of jumping.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Riley workout?", "answer": "For time: run 1.5 miles, do 150 burpees, then run 1.5 miles. CrossFit says to wear a weight vest or body armor if you have one."}, {"question": "How heavy should the vest be for Riley?", "answer": "CrossFit does not give a weight. It only says to wear a weight vest or body armor if you have one, so the vest is optional. Note what you wore with your time."}, {"question": "How far do you run in Riley?", "answer": "3 miles in total: 1.5 miles before the burpees and 1.5 miles after."}, {"question": "Who was Riley?", "answer": "U.S. Army Sgt. 1st Class Riley G. Stephens, 39, of Tolar, Texas, of the 1st Battalion, 3rd Special Forces Group (Airborne). He died on Sept. 28, 2012, in Wardak, Afghanistan."}]'::jsonb,
