For 25 minutes you do as many rounds as you can of 8 freestanding handstand push-ups and 1 L-sit rope climb to 15 feet. Both moves are high-skill gymnastics. Freestanding means no wall, so you balance every rep. In the L-sit climb you hold your legs straight out in front and climb with your arms only. Your shoulders and grip tire long before your lungs do.',
   '[{"name": "Handstand Push-Ups", "reps": "8 (freestanding)", "tip": "No wall. Kick up, find your balance, lower your head to the floor and press back up. CrossFit does not say whether kipping is allowed."}, {"name": "Rope Climbs", "reps": "1 (L-sit, to 15 ft)", "tip": "Hold your legs straight out in an L and climb with your arms only. Climb down under control."}]'::jsonb,
   'Score is total rounds + reps.',
   '["Practice freestanding handstands before you try this one", "Climb down the rope slowly to save your grip", "Rest a few breaths before each set of push-ups"]'::jsonb,
