   'Do handstand push-ups against a wall, pike push-ups on a box, or regular push-ups. Replace the L-sit climb with a regular rope climb using your legs, a shorter climb, or 3 lying-to-standing rope pulls. Newer athletes can do 15 or 20 minutes.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Robbie workout?", "answer": "As many rounds as possible in 25 minutes of 8 freestanding handstand push-ups and 1 L-sit rope climb to 15 feet."}, {"question": "What is an L-sit rope climb?", "answer": "A rope climb done with your legs held straight out in front of you, so your arms do all the work."}, {"question": "Do I need a wall for Robbie?", "answer": "No. CrossFit asks for freestanding handstand push-ups, so no wall. Use a wall only as a scaled version and note it with your score."}, {"question": "Who was Robbie?", "answer": "U.S. Army Staff Sgt. Robert J. Miller, 24, of Oviedo, Florida, of the 3rd Battalion, 3rd Special Forces Group (Airborne). He died on Jan. 25, 2008, in Bari Kowt, Afghanistan, and was awarded the Medal of Honor posthumously."}]'::jsonb,
