   'Rocket honors U.S. Army Sgt. 1st Class Aaron "Rocket" Henderson, 33, of Houlton, Maine, assigned to the 2nd Battalion, 5th Special Forces Group (Airborne). He died on Oct. 2, 2012, at Bagram Air Base, Afghanistan, of wounds suffered from an improvised explosive device in Zombalay Village, Afghanistan.

For 30 minutes you do as many rounds as you can of a 50-yard swim, 10 push-ups and 15 squats. You need a pool with room to do the push-ups and squats on the deck. The moves are simple, but climbing out of the water for each set and diving back in keeps your heart rate high for the full half hour.',
   '[{"name": "Swimming", "reps": "50 yd", "tip": "Any stroke. Swim at a pace you can repeat every round for 30 minutes."}, {"name": "Push-Ups", "reps": "10", "tip": "Chest to the deck and arms locked out at the top. Keep your body in a straight line."}, {"name": "Air Squats", "reps": "15", "tip": "Hips below your knees and stand all the way up. Wet feet slip, so stand on a dry spot."}]'::jsonb,
   'Score is total rounds + reps.',
   '["Set up your push-up and squat spot right at the end of the lane", "Swim relaxed and breathe often", "Watch your footing on a wet deck"]'::jsonb,
   '["Pick a stroke you can hold for the whole workout, such as freestyle or breaststroke.", "Climb out of the pool carefully rather than jumping out fast.", "Do the push-ups and squats unbroken if you can, and use the swim to settle your breathing.", "Swim with a lifeguard or a partner nearby, because fatigue makes swimming harder to judge.", "CrossFit does not say how to count a partial swim at the end, so decide before you start and note how you scored it."]'::jsonb,
   'Swim 25 yards, or use a kickboard. If you have no pool, replace the swim with a 200 m run and note it with your score. Do push-ups on your knees or against a raised edge, and cut the time to 20 minutes.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Rocket workout?", "answer": "As many rounds as possible in 30 minutes of a 50-yard swim, 10 push-ups and 15 squats."}, {"question": "What if I do not have a pool?", "answer": "CrossFit does not give a substitute. You could use a short run or row in place of the swim, but note the change with your score."}, {"question": "Which stroke do I use for the swim?", "answer": "CrossFit does not say, so any stroke is fine."}, {"question": "Who was Rocket?", "answer": "U.S. Army Sgt. 1st Class Aaron \"Rocket\" Henderson, 33, of Houlton, Maine, of the 2nd Battalion, 5th Special Forces Group (Airborne). He died on Oct. 2, 2012, at Bagram Air Base, Afghanistan."}]'::jsonb,
