This is a workout for a team of 3. You start with a 1,065-foot VersaClimber climb, or a 1,065 m row or ski. Then you do 10 rounds of 13 deadlifts, 13 pull-ups, a 13-calorie row, 13 back squats and 13 burpees, and finish with another 1,065-foot climb, row or ski. The barbell is 225 lb / 165 lb for both lifts. CrossFit does not say how the team splits the work, so agree on it before you start. If you or someone you know is struggling, call or text 988 (Veterans: press 1).',
   '[{"name": "Vertical Climb", "reps": "1,065 ft (or 1,065 m row or ski)", "tip": "Choose a VersaClimber, a rower or a ski machine. CrossFit does not say how to split the distance."}, {"name": "Deadlifts", "reps": "10 rounds of 13", "tip": "Flat back, bar close to your legs, stand all the way up.", "rx_men": "225 lb", "rx_women": "165 lb"}, {"name": "Pull-Ups", "reps": "10 rounds of 13", "tip": "Chin over the bar on every rep."}, {"name": "Row for Calories", "reps": "10 rounds of 13 cal", "tip": "Drive with your legs first, then pull. Keep the strokes long."}, {"name": "Back Squats", "reps": "10 rounds of 13", "tip": "Squat below parallel with your chest up. Use a rack.", "rx_men": "225 lb", "rx_women": "165 lb"}, {"name": "Burpees", "reps": "10 rounds of 13", "tip": "Chest to the floor and a small jump at the top."}, {"name": "Vertical Climb", "reps": "1,065 ft (or 1,065 m row or ski)", "tip": "The last effort. Use the same machine you chose at the start."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your team''s finish time.',
   '["Agree on how to split the work before the clock starts", "Rotate often so nobody does a big set alone", "Set up a squat rack next to the deadlift bar"]'::jsonb,
   '["A simple plan is to rotate after every movement, or to split each set of 13 into small parts such as 5, 4 and 4.", "Keep one barbell on the floor for deadlifts and one in a rack for back squats so you are not changing setups.", "At 225 lb / 165 lb, heavy back squats for 130 reps is a lot of volume, so keep every rep controlled and rack the bar before your form slips.", "Use short turns on the climb, row or ski so the team keeps a high pace.", "Pick one machine for the start and the finish so your score is easy to compare."]'::jsonb,
   'Lower the barbell to 155 lb / 105 lb or less. Use banded or jumping pull-ups. Cut to 6 or 8 rounds, or to 10 reps per movement. Shorten the climb, row or ski to 500 m. If you have a smaller team, cut the rounds to match.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Ryan Comas workout?", "answer": "For time as a team of 3: a 1,065-foot VersaClimber climb or 1,065 m row or ski, then 10 rounds of 13 deadlifts, 13 pull-ups, a 13-calorie row, 13 back squats and 13 burpees, then another 1,065-foot climb or 1,065 m row or ski. The barbell is 225 lb / 165 lb."}, {"question": "How do teams split Ryan Comas?", "answer": "CrossFit does not say. Any split works as long as the team finishes all the work. Agree on your plan before you start."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Ryan Comas?", "answer": "520 reps for the team (130 each of deadlifts, pull-ups, back squats and burpees), plus 130 calories of rowing and the two 1,065-foot climbs or 1,065 m rows or skis."}, {"question": "Who was Ryan Comas?", "answer": "U.S. Coast Guard Petty Officer 3rd Class Ryan Patrick Comas of Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, a rescue swimmer in Kodiak, Alaska. He died by suicide on June 25, 2024. If you or someone you know is struggling, call or text 988 (Veterans: press 1)."}]'::jsonb,
