   '["Take off the vest after the first run and leave it where you start the last run.", "Break the 9 power cleans into sets such as 5 and 4, or 3, 3 and 3.", "The strict pull-ups are only 2 per round, so do them fresh and clean.", "Pace the burpees so you can move straight to the next round of cleans.", "If the double-unders trip you up, take short sets of 10 to 15 rather than long misses."]'::jsonb,
   'Run without the vest or use a lighter one. Lower the barbell to 95 lb / 65 lb or less. Use banded pull-ups, a lower box or step-ups, push-ups on your knees, and 100 single-unders in place of the double-unders. Shorten each run to 800 m.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Ryan SO workout?", "answer": "For time: 1,600 m run, then 4 rounds of 9 power cleans, 2 strict pull-ups and 14 burpees, then 3 rounds of 13 box jumps, 13 push-ups and 50 double-unders, then a 1,600 m run. Wear a 20 lb / 14 lb vest for the runs. The barbell is 135 lb / 95 lb and the box is 24 in / 20 in."}, {"question": "Do I wear the vest for the whole workout?", "answer": "No. CrossFit says the vest is for the runs only."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Ryan SO?", "answer": "328 reps: 36 power cleans, 8 strict pull-ups, 56 burpees, 39 box jumps, 39 push-ups and 150 double-unders, plus 3,200 m of running."}, {"question": "Who was Ryan SO?", "answer": "Detective Ryan Yeong-Ung So, 38, of the Scottsdale, Arizona, Police Department, a U.S. Navy veteran and SWAT instructor. He died on June 13, 2024, while executing a warrant with the department''s SWAT and special assignment unit."}]'::jsonb,
