Each of the 7 rounds is 18 dumbbell hang squat cleans (35 lb / 20 lb dumbbells), 18 pull-ups, 10 barbell power cleans (135 lb / 95 lb) and 10 handstand push-ups. That adds up to 392 reps. The dumbbells and pull-ups tire your grip right before the barbell, and the handstand push-ups finish off your shoulders every round. Seven rounds is a long time to hold a steady pace.',
   '[{"name": "Dumbbell Squat Cleans", "reps": "7 rounds of 18 (from the hang)", "tip": "Start with the dumbbells at your thighs, then clean them to your shoulders and ride down into a full squat.", "rx_men": "35 lb", "rx_women": "20 lb"}, {"name": "Pull-Ups", "reps": "7 rounds of 18", "tip": "Chin over the bar on every rep. Break the set early to save your grip."}, {"name": "Power Cleans", "reps": "7 rounds of 10", "tip": "Catch the bar above parallel. Quick singles keep your form sharp when your grip is tired.", "rx_men": "135 lb", "rx_women": "95 lb"}, {"name": "Handstand Push-Ups", "reps": "7 rounds of 10", "tip": "Head to the floor and lock your arms out at the top."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Break the pull-ups before you need to", "Set up the dumbbells, bar and wall close together", "Pace the first round slower than you want to"]'::jsonb,
   '["On the dumbbell hang squat cleans, keep the dumbbells close and land with your elbows up.", "Plan the 18 pull-ups as small sets, such as 6, 6 and 6, from the first round.", "Do the power cleans as touch-and-go only while they stay smooth, then switch to singles.", "On the handstand push-ups, set your hands just wider than shoulder width and keep your core tight.", "Aim for the same split time every round rather than racing round one."]'::jsonb,
   'Use lighter dumbbells and a lighter barbell, such as 25 lb / 15 lb and 95 lb / 65 lb. Use banded pull-ups or ring rows, and pike push-ups or regular push-ups in place of handstand push-ups. Newer athletes can do 4 or 5 rounds.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Santiago workout?", "answer": "7 rounds for time of 18 dumbbell hang squat cleans, 18 pull-ups, 10 power cleans and 10 handstand push-ups. The dumbbells are 35 lb / 20 lb and the barbell is 135 lb / 95 lb."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Santiago?", "answer": "392 reps: 126 dumbbell hang squat cleans, 126 pull-ups, 70 power cleans and 70 handstand push-ups."}, {"question": "Do I use one dumbbell or two?", "answer": "CrossFit writes dumbbells, so use a pair."}, {"question": "Who was Santiago?", "answer": "U.S. Army Sgt. Anibal Santiago, 37, of Belvidere, Illinois, of the 3rd Battalion, 75th Ranger Regiment. He died on July 18, 2010, in Bagram, Afghanistan."}]'::jsonb,
