   'Schmalls honors U.S. Marine Corps Staff Sgt. Justin E. Schmalstieg, 28, of Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, assigned to the 1st Explosive Ordnance Disposal Company, 7th Engineer Support Battalion, 1st Marine Logistics Group, based at Camp Pendleton, California. He died on Dec. 15, 2010, while conducting combat operations in Helmand province, Afghanistan.

You run 800 m, then do 2 rounds of 50 burpees, 40 pull-ups, 30 single-leg squats, 20 kettlebell swings (53 lb / 35 lb) and 10 handstand push-ups, and finish with another 800 m run. The sets start huge and shrink as you go. The 100 burpees and 80 pull-ups take the most time, and the single-leg squats need balance on tired legs.',
   '[{"name": "Run", "reps": "800 m", "tip": "An easy start. Save your energy for the burpees."}, {"name": "Burpees", "reps": "2 rounds of 50", "tip": "Chest to the floor and a small jump at the top. Find a steady rhythm."}, {"name": "Pull-Ups", "reps": "2 rounds of 40", "tip": "Chin over the bar on every rep. Break the set into small parts from the start."}, {"name": "Pistol Squats", "reps": "2 rounds of 30", "tip": "CrossFit writes single-leg squats. Sit your hips all the way down on one leg and stand up without help. CrossFit does not say whether 30 is the total or per leg."}, {"name": "Kettlebell Swings", "reps": "2 rounds of 20", "tip": "Snap your hips forward and let the bell float. CrossFit does not say how high to swing.", "rx_men": "53 lb", "rx_women": "35 lb"}, {"name": "Handstand Push-Ups", "reps": "2 rounds of 10", "tip": "Head to the floor and lock your arms out at the top."}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "800 m", "tip": "Push the pace now. It is the last piece."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Pace the 50 burpees, do not race them", "Break the 40 pull-ups into small sets early", "Decide how you will count the single-leg squats before you start"]'::jsonb,
   '["Break the 50 burpees into sets of 10 with a short breath between each.", "Plan the 40 pull-ups as sets of 5 to 8 so your grip lasts for the second round.", "Alternate legs on the single-leg squats and hold onto nothing, or note it if you need support.", "On the kettlebell swings, keep your back flat and drive with your hips, not your arms.", "Count each movement out loud in the second round, because it is easy to lose track."]'::jsonb,
   'Cut each set in half (25, 20, 15, 10 and 5). Use banded pull-ups or ring rows. Do single-leg squats to a box, or air squats. Use a lighter kettlebell and replace the handstand push-ups with pike push-ups or regular push-ups.',
