   'Scotty honors firefighter Scott "Scotty" Deem, 31, of San Antonio, Texas, who served with the San Antonio Fire Department for six years. He was killed on May 18, 2017, while searching a four-alarm structure fire for survivors. He trained at the department''s CrossFit affiliate, and his favorite workouts included The Chief, DT and Lynne.

For 11 minutes you do as many rounds as you can of 5 deadlifts (315 lb / 205 lb), 18 wall-ball shots (20 lb to 10 ft / 14 lb to 9 ft) and 17 burpees over the bar. The deadlifts are heavy, so they come in quick singles. The wall balls and burpees are where you lose time, and you start every round on tired legs.',
   '[{"name": "Deadlifts", "reps": "5", "tip": "Flat back, bar close to your legs, and stand all the way up. Quick singles are fine.", "rx_men": "315 lb", "rx_women": "205 lb"}, {"name": "Wall Balls", "reps": "18", "tip": "Squat below parallel and drive the ball to the target.", "rx_men": "20 lb, 10 ft", "rx_women": "14 lb, 9 ft"}, {"name": "Burpees Over the Bar", "reps": "17", "tip": "Chest to the floor next to the bar, then jump over it. CrossFit does not say you must face the bar."}]'::jsonb,
