   'Sean honors U.S. Army Staff Sgt. Sean M. Flannery, 29, of Wyomissing, Pennsylvania, assigned to the 2nd Battalion, 502nd Infantry Regiment, 2nd Brigade Combat Team, 101st Airborne Division (Air Assault), based at Fort Campbell, Kentucky. He was killed on Nov. 22, 2010, in Kandahar Province, Afghanistan, when insurgents attacked his unit with an improvised explosive device.

Each of the 10 rounds is 11 chest-to-bar pull-ups and 22 front squats with a light barbell (75 lb / 55 lb). That adds up to 110 chest-to-bar pull-ups and 220 front squats. The weight is light, but the volume is high. Your grip and lats fade on the pull-ups, and your legs burn on the squats long before the bar feels heavy.',
   '[{"name": "Chest-to-Bar Pull-Ups", "reps": "10 rounds of 11", "tip": "Pull until your chest touches the bar. Break the set early to keep your pace."}, {"name": "Front Squats", "reps": "10 rounds of 22", "tip": "Elbows up, chest tall, and squat below parallel.", "rx_men": "75 lb", "rx_women": "55 lb"}]'::jsonb,
